      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, i'm working on a loft addition for a residential house in oregon. i'm using a douglas fir beam for the main support. the span is gonna be about 14 feet and i'm expecting a dead load of roughly 15 lbs per sq ft plus a live load of 30 lbs per sq ft. can you help me figure out if a single 4x12 is enough for deflection limits or if i need to step up to something bigger?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
