      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Ah, a loft addition, a noble endeavor indeed! Now, let's talk about those Douglas fir beams, sturdy as a goblin's resolve. With a span of 14 feet, you're looking at a considerable distance, much like a goblin's long journey to the enchanted forest. The dead load of 15 lbs per sq ft and the live load of 30 lbs per sq ft, combined, give us a total of 45 lbs per sq ft. A single 4x12 beam, however, might be akin to a single goblin trying to carry a mountain of gold – not quite enough, my friend.\n\nTo ensure your loft doesn't sag like a goblin's belly after a feast, you might need to step up to a larger beam, perhaps a 6x12 or even a 8x12. These would be like a band of goblins, stronger together, capable of carrying the weight of your dreams and the load of your loft addition. Remember, in the world of construction, as in goblin lore, it's always better to be safe than sorry.",
